from VK:
Had such a case from practice. A patient fell in love with me. And she was, well, totally-totally-totally!!! not my type, like not at all. The piquancy of the situation was that she was the subject of my dissertation, and I was to work with her for at least 2 more years. So, you can't just use and ditch her. Had to reject her and diplomatically freeze her out, so as not to lose a patient with an excellent functional result.
In the end she moved to another country and married a foreigner. And as a keepsake I have photos of her legs. X-ray ones )))

from a forum, traffic police questions:
kuka22# - Can you pass the category B exam without studying at a driving school? By cistern?
Marsmensch - If you take it by canister, it's easy. And if by cistern, they'll surely give you all categories.

from the discussion "how do you feel about a guy being younger than the girl":
El Dolor:
I liked girls who were older than me, because I saw in each of them my protectoress and support. But none suited me, I was afraid to confess my "feelings", thought I couldn't bear the worries. I fell in love most often with fictional characters. I remember that once at 13 I fell in love with a girl who was on the poster of the game "SpellForce: order of dawn". She combined both darkness and light, and most importantly, - she held a sword in her hands, which was already considered by me as protection.

